# Rank 1150 / CVE-2026-25083: GROWI's OpenAI thread and message routes looked
# up a ThreadRelation by threadId alone, so a logged-in user who learned a
# shared AI assistant's thread id could read or post into another user's
# thread (CWE-862). postMessageHandlersFactory and its siblings
# (get-messages, get-threads, delete-thread, edit) called
#
#   const threadRelation = await ThreadRelationModel.findOne({ threadId });
#
# with threadId taken straight from req.body/req.params and no filter tying
# the row to req.user. Commit 236549a47e273afe23846e425bcc93918c67ee17 is the
# real fix, found from GHSA-c69x-9x9c-p9v7 and the growi.co.jp advisory
# naming v7.4.6: it adds userId: user._id to every ThreadRelationModel query
# and to getThreadsByAiAssistantId's and deleteThread's signatures. The pool
# row named 042c50f01f8f6c1d0c4e5140d4079fa0bf8603a2, a same-day commit
# titled "delete changes to openai.ts from master" that only reverts an
# unrelated refactor in a helper method never called; replaced in place with
# 236549a47e273afe23846e425bcc93918c67ee17, the commit "fix: openai thread
# idor" whose diff matches the advisory exactly.
#
# ATTENTION, vocabulary gap. Scanning either revision reports the same seven
# VYQL-CFG-014 rows plus one VYQL-RF-003 row, all in unrelated login and
# page-listing code; vyql match confirms req.body is labelled code.HttpInput
# at the threadId destructure but ThreadRelationModel.findOne itself carries
# no sink or check label in either revision. code.IdorPolicyReview (VYQL-AUTH-
# 081) is the right concept and already has JavaScript bindings, but every one
# of them keys on a presence match naming one project's identifiers (a Prisma
# accounts.update call missing "currentUserId", a phpReview marker string),
# not on the general shape "a query object literal missing an ownership key".
# Stating that shape as a binding without naming this project's userId/
# ThreadRelationModel would need the engine to reason about which fields an
# object literal omits relative to a schema it has never seen, which is the
# same flat-bag negation already declined at ranks 1074 and 1081 for the same
# reason: a collection lookup that legitimately owns every row it returns has
# an identical shape. No definition change attempted.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-vocabulary-gap, both revisions rejected.

test "rank1150: thread lookup keyed only by threadId, no owner filter"
  lang javascript
  reject VYQL-AUTH-081
  reject_review code.IdorPolicyReview
  code
  ```
  export const postMessageHandlersFactory = (crowi) => {
    return [
      loginRequiredStrictly,
      certifyAiService,
      async (req, res) => {
        const { user } = req;
        const { aiAssistantId, threadId } = req.body;

        const aiAssistant = await AiAssistantModel.findById(aiAssistantId);
        if (aiAssistant == null) {
          return res.apiv3Err(new ErrorV3('AI assistant not found'), 404);
        }

        const threadRelation = await ThreadRelationModel.findOne({ threadId });
        if (threadRelation == null) {
          return res.apiv3Err(new ErrorV3('ThreadRelation not found'), 404);
        }

        return streamMessageToThread(threadRelation, user);
      },
    ];
  };
  ```

test "rank1150: thread lookup scoped to the requesting user's id"
  lang javascript
  reject VYQL-AUTH-081
  reject_review code.IdorPolicyReview
  code
  ```
  export const postMessageHandlersFactory = (crowi) => {
    return [
      loginRequiredStrictly,
      certifyAiService,
      async (req, res) => {
        const { user } = req;
        const { aiAssistantId, threadId } = req.body;

        const aiAssistant = await AiAssistantModel.findById(aiAssistantId);
        if (aiAssistant == null) {
          return res.apiv3Err(new ErrorV3('AI assistant not found'), 404);
        }

        const threadRelation = await ThreadRelationModel.findOne({
          threadId,
          userId: user._id,
        });
        if (threadRelation == null) {
          return res.apiv3Err(new ErrorV3('ThreadRelation not found'), 404);
        }

        return streamMessageToThread(threadRelation, user);
      },
    ];
  };
  ```
